flowchart TD
  accTitle: Every thread can orchestrate. One optional project role.
  accDescr: Proposed UX: outcome threads can start directly. One ordinary thread may be designated to coordinate priorities and shared decisions for an explicit project scope. Dashed arrows mean optional coordination, not a prerequisite to launch an outcome. The current create/resume binding is checkout-local; arbitrary existing-thread assignment and revision-checked reassignment are proposed. Reassignment preserves active attempts. A role grants no extra authority.
  scope --> coordinator
  coordinator -.-> outcome_a
  coordinator -.-> outcome_b
  coordinator -.-> outcome_c
  outcome_a --> tasks_a
  outcome_b --> tasks_b
  outcome_c --> tasks_c
  tasks_a --> evidence
  tasks_b --> evidence
  tasks_c --> evidence
  scope["Explicit project scope"]
  coordinator["One designated ordinary thread"]
  outcome_a["Outcome thread A"]
  outcome_b["Outcome thread B"]
  outcome_c["Outcome thread C"]
  tasks_a["Own tasks / collaborators"]
  tasks_b["Own tasks / collaborators"]
  tasks_c["Own tasks / collaborators"]
  evidence["Results + project decisions"]
